  "text": "Good morning everyone. This is the weekly engineering sync for Project Nimbus. Today is Thursday, and we have four items on the agenda. The Kubernetes migration, the PostgreSQL latency issue, the Q3 OKRs, and the hiring update. Priya, do you want to start? with the migration. Sure, thanks Marcus. So the kubernetes migration is about 70% done. We moved the authentication service, and the billing service to the new EKS cluster last week. The main blocker right now is the RIDIZ cache. When we deployed it with... The persistent volume claims were failing because of a misconfigured storage class. I opened a ticket, here a number n-i-m-pash-4-8-2, and I expect it to be fixed by Tuesday. Okay, good. Do we need anything from the DevOps team? Yes, we need Thomas to approve the Terraform changes for the VPC peering. Without that, the pods in the staging namespace cannot reach the legacy database. I can review the Terraform pull request this afternoon. I saw it in GitHub yesterday, but I did not have time. Just to confirm, are we still using the T3 large instances for the worker nodes, or did we switch to Graviton? We switched to Graviton. The ARM-based instances are about 20% cheaper, and our Docker images now build for both architectures. Great. Let's move to item 2, the PostgreSQL latency issue. Thomas, what did you find? So, the P99 latency on the order endpoint went from about 80 milliseconds to almost 400 milliseconds after the release on the 12th. I ran X-Player.",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.139999866485596,
      "text": "Good morning everyone. This is the weekly engineering sync for Project Nimbus. Today"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.139999866485596,
      "end": 13.0600004196167,
      "text": "is Thursday, and we have four items on the agenda. The Kubernetes migration, the PostgreSQL"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.0600004196167,
      "end": 19.979999542236328,
      "text": "latency issue, the Q3 OKRs, and the hiring update. Priya, do you want to start?"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.0,
      "end": 20.9200000166893,
      "text": "with the migration."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.460000038146973,
      "end": 24.09999990463257,
      "text": "Sure, thanks Marcus."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.59999990463257,
      "end": 28.539999961853027,
      "text": "So the kubernetes migration is about 70% done."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.9399995803833,
      "end": 31.31999969482422,
      "text": "We moved the authentication service,"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.520000457763672,
      "end": 35.5,
      "text": "and the billing service to the new EKS cluster last week."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.579999923706055,
      "end": 38.13999938964844,
      "text": "The main blocker right now is the RIDIZ cache."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.579999923706055,
      "end": 39.97999954223633,
      "text": "When we deployed it with..."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.0,
      "end": 45.96000003814697,
      "text": "The persistent volume claims were failing because of a misconfigured storage class."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.44000005722046,
      "end": 53.34000015258789,
      "text": "I opened a ticket, here a number n-i-m-pash-4-8-2, and I expect it to be fixed by Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.72000026702881,
      "end": 58.70000076293945,
      "text": "Okay, good. Do we need anything from the DevOps team?"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.0,
      "end": 65.09999990463257,
      "text": "Yes, we need Thomas to approve the Terraform changes for the VPC peering."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.69999980926514,
      "end": 70.84000015258789,
      "text": "Without that, the pods in the staging namespace cannot reach the legacy database."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.14000034332275,
      "end": 75.53999996185303,
      "text": "I can review the Terraform pull request this afternoon."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.97999954223633,
      "end": 79.71999931335449,
      "text": "I saw it in GitHub yesterday, but I did not have time."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.0,
      "end": 87.80000019073486,
      "text": "Just to confirm, are we still using the T3 large instances for the worker nodes, or did we switch to Graviton?"
    },
    {
      "start": 88.68000030517578,
      "end": 98.78000068664551,
      "text": "We switched to Graviton. The ARM-based instances are about 20% cheaper, and our Docker images now build for both architectures."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.0,
      "end": 104.98000001907349,
      "text": "Great. Let's move to item 2, the PostgreSQL latency issue."
    },
    {
      "start": 105.5,
      "end": 107.5,
      "text": "Thomas, what did you find?"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.77999973297119,
      "end": 115.26000022888184,
      "text": "So, the P99 latency on the order endpoint went from about 80 milliseconds to almost"
    },
    {
      "start": 115.42000007629395,
      "end": 119.13999938964844,
      "text": "400 milliseconds after the release on the 12th."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.13999938964844,
      "end": 119.97999954223633,
      "text": "I ran X-Player."
    }
  ],
